der and chest after rain. Wet fur reflects emerald leaves turquoise sky and warm orange sunset. Water droplets across the animal catch tiny environmental reflections preventing the black subject from becoming visually flat','A womans back becomes an extraordinary realistic transition from underwater to sky. Deep cobalt water begins low on the back with a realistic whale moving through it. Approaching the shoulder blades the water surface becomes visible from beneath. Above it warm orange sunset and pink clouds occupy the upper back. Light penetrates through the surface and creates believable shafts of warm color through the blue water below connecting both worlds through real physics rather than collage','Create the ultimate contemporary Colour Realism body composition. A mans shoulder and arm become one continuous believable world at the boundary between tropical forest and ocean. A brilliantly colored kingfisher launches from emerald foliage across the shoulder toward turquoise water flowing down the arm. Orange sunlight from behind the bird illuminates feather edges leaves and water while the shadow side receives cool cobalt reflected color. Water droplets reflect the surrounding greens blues and oranges. A portion of the forearm becomes submerged allowing color temperature refraction and underwater light to transform the composition as it travels downward. Do not separate the subjects into collage panels. Every element must exist under the same believable light and atmosphere. The body must determine cropping direction and depth. From several feet away it should feel like an impossible window into a real living world')
$b['Two wet cherries hang from one stem rendered so realistically that the deep-red skin appears translucent around the highlights. Tiny condensation droplets magnify the cherry surface beneath them while reflected window light creates cool blue-white highlights'] = 'The tattoo: Two wet cherries hang from one stem, rendered so realistically that the deep-red skin appears translucent around the highlights. Tiny condensation droplets magnify the cherry surface beneath them while reflected window light creates cool blue-white highlights. Delicious, glossy, irresistible. Create exceptional contemporary Colour Realism tattoo artwork whose primary goal is convincing visual reality rendered through believable full color. Do not create an ordinary realism tattoo and simply add bright colors afterward. Build form through color, value, temperature, light, shadow, texture, reflection and atmosphere. REALISM MAKES IT BELIEVABLE. COLOR MAKES IT ALIVE. LIGHT MAKES THE COLOR MAKE SENSE. Begin every artwork with a strong value structure. Establish the primary light source, shadow structure, focal hierarchy and environmental light before determining saturation. Color must describe the physical world. Warm light should influence nearby surfaces. Cool environments should produce believable cool reflected color. Red fabric may cast subtle red into nearby skin. Green foliage may influence adjacent surfaces. Blue water should affect submerged objects and shadowed undersides. Neon must illuminate nearby skin and materials. Glass must transmit, distort and refract surrounding colors. Chrome must reflect its environment. Wet surfaces should carry believable reflections. Translucent petals, fruit, skin, water and other materials should transmit light appropriately. Use realistic color temperature throughout shadows rather than filling shadows with black. Preserve strong dark, middle and light values so the tattoo remains dimensional and readable. Vibrant does not mean uncontrolled. Saturation should support focal hierarchy. Some artwork may be intensely colorful. Some should use natural restrained color. Some may be predominantly warm or cool. Some may use muted environments with one extraordinary focal color. Suppress unnecessary hard outlines. Form should primarily emerge through changes in value, temperature, edge, texture and depth rather than graphic borders. Use sharp detail selectively at focal points and softer edges in supporting areas. Avoid making every square centimeter equally detailed. Render materials according to their real physical behavior. Skin must look like skin. Fur must follow growth direction and catch light naturally. Feathers must display believable structure and iridescence. Glass must refract. Water must distort and reflect. Metal must respond to the surrounding environment. Flowers and fruit should show translucency, moisture and surface variation where appropriate. Fabric should respond to weave, sheen and folds. The subject can be anything capable of believable rendering: portraits, human figures, animals, birds, insects, flowers, fruit, ocean, landscapes, objects, glass, chrome, fabric, architecture, cinematic scenes, surreal concepts and impossible worlds. Surreal imagery is fully allowed, but impossible subjects must still obey convincing light, material, perspective and atmospheric logic. Do not reduce Colour Realism to endless lions, tigers, womens faces, roses and eyes. Use those subjects when the artwork is exceptional, but explore the full world. Design specifically for the stated body placement. Do not paste rectangular photographs onto skin. Crop compositions naturally. Let subjects enter and leave the body area without artificial frames. Use shoulder curvature to enhance dimensional subjects. Let forearms and calves support strong vertical compositions. Give portraits, animals and complex scenes sufficient room. Use thighs for more detailed compositions and backs, chests and sleeves for the rare larger narrative work. Anatomy should influence movement, crop and visual hierarchy. Do not make every tattoo enormous. Most concepts should remain attainable small and medium pieces while retaining enough physical size for realistic color transitions and detail. Use fewer large pieces and only rare major body compositions. Avoid artificial HDR, plastic-looking skin, excessive saturation, neon colors without a believable light source, generic blurred backgrounds, unnecessary black outlines, flat color fill, muddy midtones, random color splashes, photographic rectangles, unrelated collage elements and impossible reflections that ignore environmental logic. IF THE TATTOO WOULD BE JUST AS POWERFUL IN BLACK AND GREY, ASK WHETHER COLOR IS ACTUALLY CONTRIBUTING SOMETHING IMPORTANT. COLOR SHOULD REVEAL SOMETHING BLACK AND GREY COULD NOT. REALISM MAKES IT BELIEVABLE. COLOR MAKES IT ALIVE. LIGHT MAKES THE COLOR MAKE SENSE. In the right panel it is on a woman, inner forearm, giving the small still life enough clean space for the droplets and reflections to read. The right panel is one single photograph of one person showing that one area once. The whole image has exactly two panels'
